    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` + `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the owner contract while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerates the DTOs)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to `OwnerFields`; these flow into both the request and the `Owner` response (which is `allOf OwnerFields`).\n- Made the flat `address` optional: dropped `@NotBlank` (kept `@AddressValidation`, which only rejects a *supplied* blank value) and removed `address` from the `required` list.\n- Added a new class-level `@AddressFormValidation` constraint alongside the existing `@PostcodeValidation`.\n\n**Validation (`rest/validation/`)**\n- New `AddressFormValidation` + `AddressFormValidator`: a payload is valid when it has a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address` (blankness decided via `AddressNormalizer`). City is still required via its own `@NotBlank`. Minimal flat-address owners still pass.\n\n**Mapping (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`)**\n- `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` are normalized (same rules as the flat address) and stored.\n- `address` is now composed via `composeAddress(...)`: when `addressLine1` is present it becomes the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when present; otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`. Storing the composed value in `owner.address` means everything that reads the address (locality, household/customer-code logic, the returned `address`) transparently uses the structured fields when present and the flat address otherwise.\n\n**Model & schema**\n- `Owner.java`: added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` columns + accessors; removed `@NotEmpty` from `address`.\n- Added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns to all four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres); relaxed the h2 `address NOT NULL` since the field is now optional.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 structured-address normalization/composition, and the flat-address backward-compat case \u2014 both pass.",
